>> source: https://www.traderjoes.com/home/recipes/mezza-luna-lasagna
>> tags: [ pasta, trader-joes, dinner, squash, lasagna ]
>> time: 2 hours 15 minutes
>> servings: 6-8

Preheat oven to 375°F. Slice @butternut squash (peeled, sliced lengthwise and cleaned of seeds and string){1%large} halves into 1/2-inch half-moon-shaped pieces. Spray a large baking sheet with a light dusting of @olive oil cooking spray{} and sprinkle with a little @sea salt{} and @black pepper{}. Place the slices on the sheet in a single layer. Lightly spray the tops and sprinkle with salt and pepper. Bake until the slices are tender, ~{35%minutes}. Remove from oven and set aside to cool; lower oven temperature to 350°F.

Empty @Alfredo sauce{2%jars} into a sauce pan; warm over very low heat, just enough to liquefy, and remove from heat. Place @ricotta cheese{15%oz}, @frozen spinach (chopped, defrosted and squeezed of some water){2%cups}, @nutmeg{1/4%tsp} and a pinch of salt into a bowl and combine. Set aside.

Assemble lasagna: Coat the bottom of a 9x13-inch baking dish with a light layer of Alfredo sauce. Place four sheets of @no boil lasagna noodles{12%sheets} side by side and top them with more Alfredo sauce. Next, add squash in a single layer. Top squash with more Alfredo sauce and another layer of noodles. Top noodles with all of the ricotta-spinach mixture and smooth out. Top with another layer of noodles, then Alfredo sauce and the last of the squash. Pour over the remainder of Alfredo sauce and top with @mozzarella cheese (shredded){1%cup} and @Parmigiano Reggiano cheese (grated){1/2%cup}.

Cover lasagna with foil and bake for ~{40%minutes}. Remove foil and bake another ~{10%minutes} or until cheese is golden and bubbly. Remove from oven and rest ~{15%minutes} before slicing.
